PHP 7.4 ext/gd: the GD build test's conftest must return a value

`PHP_TEST_BUILD` (build/php.m4) is AC_RUN_IFELSE — it compiles, links AND RUNS
the program. ext/gd/config.m4 hands it `char foobar () {}`: a non-void function
that falls off the end, which is undefined behaviour in C.

Old compilers let that return garbage harmlessly. clang 16+ emits a trap
instruction at the end of a non-void function with no return, so the conftest
dies where it stands:

    ./configure: line 2481: 38377 Illegal instruction: 4  ./conftest
    configure:36285: $? = 132
    configure: error: GD build test failed. Please check the config.log for details.

Nothing is wrong with gd, with libpng, or with any of the ~40 libraries on that
link line — which is what makes the message expensive. It names an extension and
a "build test", and the failure is neither. It cost two builds and one wrong
diagnosis before the config.log artifact showed the exit status: 132 is SIGILL,
and a compile error cannot produce it.

Homebrew's php@7.4 never hits this because the formula carries `fails_with
:clang` and builds with GCC, where falling off the end stays benign. We build
with Apple clang, so the source has to be correct rather than lucky.

This is the ONLY occurrence in the tree:
    grep -rn '() {}' ext/*/config.m4  →  ext/gd/config.m4:176

--- a/ext/gd/config.m4	2026-08-14 22:43:35
+++ b/ext/gd/config.m4	2026-08-14 22:43:35
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@
 
     PHP_TEST_BUILD(foobar, [], [
       AC_MSG_ERROR([GD build test failed. Please check the config.log for details.])
-    ], [ $GD_SHARED_LIBADD ], [char foobar () {}])
+    ], [ $GD_SHARED_LIBADD ], [char foobar () { return 0; }])
 
   else
     extra_sources="gd_compat.c"
